<title>AUSTRIA: TABLE-RHI H1 profit up, sees strong full-yr.</title>
<headline>TABLE-RHI H1 profit up, sees strong full-yr.</headline>
<dateline>VIENNA 1997-07-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Period to June 30, 1997.</p>
<p>(figures in millions of schillings unless otherwise stated)</p>
<p>					1997		1996</p>
<p> Group sales		    10,265	    10,372</p>
<p> Group operating		   323		 343</p>
<p> Group pre-tax		     220		 208</p>
<p> Group net			   174		 153</p>
<p> Group net (after minorities)  169		 156</p>
<p> Group operative cash flow     524		 351</p>
<p> Investments			 269		 409</p>
<p> Workforce (on June 30)     10,704	    10,898</p>
<p>NOTE - Full company name is Radex-Heraklith, which changes to RHI January 1, 1998. It has a 57.6 percent stake in Germany's Didier.</p>
<p>NOTE - Radex said &quot;it should be possible&quot; for the group to achieve a return on sales of four percent for the full-year, up from 3.2 percent in 1996.</p>
<p>&quot;The positive trend in the second quarter confirms management in its expectation that the full-year will show a further rise in earnings,&quot; it said in a statement. Fireproof/engineering division</p>
